@ 17.7.2.3 - Middle High German to Standard German
# citation: Paweł Ciupak, from Behr, Hans-Joahim, Ingrid Bennewitz, et al. (2004). Die Bamberg (BA)-Braunschweiger (BS) Grammatik des Alt- und Mittelhochdeutschen im Internet. <https://www.tu-braunschweig.de/Medien-DB/germanistik/babs260304.pdf>; Kundert, Ursula (2009). Einführung in das Mittelhochdeutsche. <http://www.germsem.uni-kiel.de/mediaevistik/materialien/Kundert_Mhdreader_090330.pdf>; and Anonymous (2009). Mittelhochdeutsche Kurzgrammatik. <https://www.uni-frankfurt.de/47053276/Kurzgrammatik-HA_09_2009.pdf>
	s > ʃ / :{ #_l, #_m, #_n, #_w, #_p, #_t }:
	s > ʃ / r_
	t > t͡s, k / _w
	x > k / _s
	{h,j} > ∅ / V_V
	{ w, j } > { b, ɡ } / :{ l_ (occasionally otherwise), r_ (occasionally otherwise) }:
	w > ∅ / :{ ou_, øy_, y:[+long]_ }:
	w > v
	a:[+long] > o:[+long] / :{ _N(sporadic?), _C:[+dental](sporadic?), _P(sporadic?), _h(sporadic?) }:
	a:[+long] > o:[+long] / :{ N_ (sporadic?), C:[+dental]_ (sporadic?), P_ (sporadic?), h_ (sporadic?) }:
	{ {, e,, e:[+long], }, i } > { {, ø,, ø:[+long], }, y } / _C:[+affricate]
	{ {, e,, e:[+long], }, i } > { {, ø,, ø:[+long], }, y } / :{ _P(sporadic?), _l(sporadic?), _ʃ(sporadic?) }:
	{ {, e,, e:[+long], }, i } > { {, ø,, ø:[+long], }, y } / :{ P_ (sporadic?), l_ (sporadic?), ʃ_ (sporadic?) }:
	{ y, y:[+long] } yə { ø, ø:[+long] } øy > { i, i:[+long] } iə { e, e:[+long] } ei (intermittent)
	{ u:[+long], y:[+long], i:[+long] } > { ou, øy, ei } // in certain unstressed endings and monosyllables, _C{C,V,#} (especially before /xt/), and Low German borrowings
	{ uə, yə, iə } > { u:[+long], y:[+long], i:[+long] }
	{ ou, øy, ei } > { au, oy, ai }
	{ u, y } > { o, ø } / _N (with some occasional exceptions)
	a:[+long]w > au
	V:[+long] > V:[-long] / _CC (some exceptions; the change was more common around _xt and _rC)
	V:[+long] > V:[-long] / _%Cə{r,l,n}# (some exceptions)
	V > V:[+long] / _%, (except for /ə/?)
	V > V:[+long] / _r{t,d,s,t͡s} (except /ə/)
	V > V:[+long] / in some monosyllables ending in alveolar resonant͡s or vowels
	V > V:[+long] / by analogy in some cases
	ə > ∅ / unstressed, but not in every case
	∅ > ə / M_r% (I don’t know what Mr. Ciupak means by 〈M〉)